WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.781
Here we compare two different policies The first
query uses ordinary

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:10.744
not equal to Paid If payment status is null that
comparison becomes

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:15.409
UNKNOWN so the row is filtered out The second query
uses IS

00:00:15.435 --> 00:00:19.881
DISTINCT FROM Paid Now a missing status is treated
as different from

00:00:19.906 --> 00:00:24.133
Paid and the record is included Run both queries in
the browser

00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:28.579
and compare the results You should see one important
difference caused by

00:00:28.592 --> 00:00:33.218
the null status You can also copy the queries into
pgAdmin and

00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:38.115
run them separately Neither query is automatically
the right query for every

00:00:38.141 --> 00:00:43.347
situation The correct choice depends on the question
Do we mean a

00:00:43.373 --> 00:00:46.388
status that is known and not Paid or do we mean
anything

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:47.870
that is not definitely Paid
